        "original_id": "c2f85b98-450b-5667-9070-032bc2c642cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: W. Somerset Maugham, Thomas Merton\n- Works: Liza of Lambeth\n- Roles: playwright, novelist, short story writer, Catholic writer, theologian, mystic, priest, doctor\n- Places: Lambeth, London\n\nFacts:\n- W. Somerset Maugham was born on 25 January 1874 and died on 16 December 1965.\n- W. Somerset Maugham was a British playwright, novelist, and short story writer.\n- In 1897, W. Somerset Maugham published Liza of Lambeth as his first novel.\n- W. Somerset Maugham wrote Liza of Lambeth while working as a doctor at a hospital in Lambeth, a working-class district of London.\n- During the 1930s, W. Somerset Maugham was reputedly the highest-paid author and was among the most popular writers of his era.\n- Thomas Merton was born on 31 January 1915 and died on 10 December 1968.\n- Thomas Merton was an American Catholic writer, theologian, and mystic.\n- In 1949, Thomas Merton was ordained to the priesthood and was given the name Father Louis.",
